WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.898
Track one operator's footsteps for an hour.

00:00:05.178 --> 00:00:09.518
The lines you draw show exactly where your station design is costing time.

00:00:10.118 --> 00:00:13.772
Walking, reaching and searching add nothing to the product,

00:00:13.772 --> 00:00:16.373
yet they fill a large part of every shift.

00:00:16.653 --> 00:00:18.405
Lean calls this motion waste.

00:00:19.005 --> 00:00:22.581
To design it out, bring everything the task needs to the station.

00:00:22.861 --> 00:00:28.758
Put tools on a pegboard, parts in bins in assembly order, power on a rail, and light on the work.

00:00:29.038 --> 00:00:33.731
Use trolleys or flow racks to bring materials in, so the operator never leaves.

00:00:34.011 --> 00:00:37.261
Then walk the station again and count the steps you removed.

00:00:37.861 --> 00:00:42.254
A bearing manufacturer we equipped placed tools, packing materials,

00:00:42.254 --> 00:00:47.303
power and the sealing machine at every station, with pallets right beside it,

00:00:47.303 --> 00:00:50.385
removing unnecessary movement and waiting time.

00:00:50.985 --> 00:00:53.861
Design the station so the operator stays put.

00:00:54.141 --> 00:00:55.992
What is your longest walk on the line?

00:00:56.272 --> 00:01:00.251
Comment below, and next, see how we go from requirement to layout.

00:01:00.851 --> 00:01:05.096
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

